depgraph: replay _iter_match_pkgs_atom results across backtracking runs

Sub-series: A (probe, match and config memos) - patch 2 of 10; applies to 3.0.83 with only the earlier patches of this sub-series.
Of these it needs none: it also applies to 3.0.83 by itself.

Every backtracking run asks for the matches of the same atoms again. The
result depends on the arguments and on state shared by all runs through
_frozen_config, except when onlydeps is set or the package has a recorded
USE change; in those two cases the memo is bypassed. Filled lazily.

Alone on 3.0.83 (three states measured): start 119.6 -> 108.6,
masks 91.0 -> 75.0, base 29.1 -> 26.2.
Least-checked change of the first three: plan identity only, no lock-step,
and no state with autounmask USE changes was run.
On upstream head it needs regenerating (context only); 114.4 -> 105.5 s there.

Origin: written by AI agents (Claude) in the emerge-fast job, 2026-11-17..20;
isolated from the full patch and measured on 2026-11-20. Not a human-written
change. Base: Portage 3.0.83. Test: `emerge -p -uND @world` on six states of
one system image, one resolve at a time; every run gave the same merge list
in the same order, the same number of backtracking attempts and the same
package count as unpatched 3.0.83.
